{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778520672,"nonce":"7+jYErEv1818OtdpwUcxjOqnjd0=","title":"Migrate Claude Code hook scripts (claude-notify, mandible-inbox-check) from dotfiles to Mandible","message":"## Goal\n\nMove Claude Code hook scripts (`claude-notify.sh`, `claude-notify-dismiss.sh`, `claude-notify-picker.sh`, `claude-notify-callback.sh`, and the obsolete `mandible-inbox-check.sh`) from `~/.dotfiles/.config/scripts/` into Mandible. Conceptually parallel to the CLI-tooling migration discussion in `c786f61` / closed umbrella `3f017f1`: these scripts are Mandible operational tools — they already read settings via `localhost:19420/api/settings` — and they should ship with Mandible for the same distribution reasons (Tauri Level 2 `fdc0e8a`, version coupling, single-source-of-truth).\n\nSurfaced from the inbox-channel design discussion (`4e32923`). The `mandible-inbox-check.sh` script becomes obsolete entirely when `4e32923` lands (the scoped session-start hook in Mandible replaces it), so its removal is also tracked here.\n\nCross-ref: rlrmp `1d9ae6f`.\n\n## Current state\n\n`~/.dotfiles/.config/scripts/` contains:\n\n- `claude-notify.sh` — `Stop`-hook notification (alerter on macOS, notify-send on Linux). Quiet hours, settings via Mandible API, multiplexer integration (zellij/tmux), session tracking via `~/.cache/claude-notify/sessions.jsonl`, click-to-navigate.\n- `claude-notify-dismiss.sh` — `UserPromptSubmit`-hook companion that clears waiting notifications when the user types.\n- `claude-notify-picker.sh`, `claude-notify-callback.sh` — supporting scripts for the click-to-navigate flow.\n- `mandible-inbox-check.sh` — the inbox dump (obsoleted by `4e32923`).\n\nWiring is in `~/.dotfiles/.config/claude/settings.json` under `Stop` and `UserPromptSubmit` hooks.\n\n## Options\n\n### Option A — relocate as bash scripts to `mandible/bin/`\n\nMove the scripts into the Mandible repo. Dotfiles `settings.json` references the new paths. Per `c786f61`'s recommended strategy, Mandible's `bin/` ends up on PATH.\n\n- **Pros**: minimal change, scripts already work, fast to do.\n- **Cons**: still ships bash scripts (slightly awkward for Tauri sidecar bundling); still requires `settings.json` edits in dotfiles.\n\n### Option B — reimplement in TypeScript inside the daemon\n\nMove notification logic into Mandible's daemon process; daemon emits native OS notifications via Node bindings (or via Tauri's notification API). Hook scripts become tiny stubs that POST to a Mandible endpoint, or are eliminated entirely if Mandible can detect session lifecycle without a hook.\n\n- **Pros**: cleaner distribution (Tauri can bundle a single binary); centralized state; native OS notification APIs are well-supported in Node/Tauri.\n- **Cons**: more code; need cross-platform native bindings; loses existing bash logic for quiet hours and multiplexer awareness (need to reimplement).\n\n### Option C — hybrid\n\nBash scripts move to `mandible/bin/` (Option A), with daemon-side notification emission added for SDK-managed sessions (Option B). Both surfaces share the same settings store. Bash scripts handle CLI/channel/external tier sessions; daemon-direct notifications handle first-class SDK sessions.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nStart with Option A (relocate-as-is) — low risk, immediate distribution benefit, no behaviour change. Defer Option B's daemon-side reimplementation until Tauri Level 2 (`fdc0e8a`) is actually being built; at that point Option C falls out naturally.\n\n## In scope of this issue\n\n1. Move the four `claude-notify*.sh` scripts from `~/.dotfiles/.config/scripts/` to `mandible/bin/` (or `mandible/scripts/`).\n2. Move the `zellij-helper.sh` and `tmux-helper.sh` siblings that `claude-notify-dismiss.sh` sources (verify which other scripts depend on them).\n3. Delete `mandible-inbox-check.sh` — obsoleted by `4e32923`.\n4. Dotfiles change: update `~/.dotfiles/.config/claude/settings.json` to reference the new paths under Mandible (or rely on PATH lookup if Mandible's bin/ is added to PATH).\n5. Documentation: update Mandible's README to describe these as part of the supported integration surface.\n\n## Out of scope (separate issues)\n\n- Option B's daemon-side reimplementation (file separately when Tauri Level 2 is in flight).\n- Channel-event vs logging-message delivery for the MCP channel (separate concern — file separately if/when we decide to enable auto-respond on inbound auth events).\n- Adding new notification triggers (auth-resolved, work-assigned, etc.).\n\n## Agent interaction tier consideration\n\nPer Mandible's CLAUDE.md, the `Stop`-hook notification is meaningful for **channel** and **external** tier sessions (Claude CLI in a terminal). First-class SDK sessions managed by Mandible can in principle emit native notifications directly from the daemon, without any hook script. The migration should keep CLI/channel sessions working as today; SDK-session-specific notification paths can be added later under Option B/C without breaking this.\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- Sibling concept to `c786f61` and the closed umbrella `3f017f1` (CLI tooling distribution).\n- Related to closed dotfiles issue `0be9711` (Notifications not appearing — verified resolved 2026-03-02; this migration preserves that working state).\n- Surfaced from `4e32923` (inbox channel scoping); the `mandible-inbox-check.sh` deletion is in scope of this issue rather than that one.\n- rlrmp meta coord: `1d9ae6f`.","files":null}]}